# Local environment. Copy to .env.local (gitignored, never committed) and fill in.
# Python reads .env.local from the repo root; real environment variables win over it.
# Production's URLs never go here: they live only in .env.live, which scripts read only when
# passed explicitly (--env-file .env.live; docs/02 › Environments & databases). That file holds
# one line, PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=… (production's direct URL; README › Releasing).
# The block at the end lists the variables that live only in Vercel or GitHub, and where.

# ─── Databases (Neon) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon `dev` branch. Pooled (host ends in "-pooler"): what the API reads at runtime.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
# Neon `dev` branch, direct (no "-pooler"): migrations (pnpm db:migrate) and ingest/publish,
# which PgBouncer's transaction mode can't serve.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# Neon `test` branch, direct URL. Tests, the fixture seed (pnpm db:seed) and e2e use only this,
# and refuse if it's unset or names the same database as DATABASE_URL. No fallback.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-yyyy.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ─── Data sources ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CFBD API key (Patreon tier 1, 5,000 calls/month). Used only by `pnpm ingest:games` for now.
CFBD_API_KEY=

# ─── Sign-in (Auth.js + GitHub) ── Next reads this file through web/next.config.ts ─────────
# Signs and encrypts the session cookie. Generate with `npx auth secret` or
# `openssl rand -base64 33`. Use a value of its own here: never production's or preview's.
AUTH_SECRET=
# The "CFB Model (dev)" GitHub OAuth app (callback http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github).
# Not the production app: its only callback is the production domain.
AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=
# The one GitHub account allowed in: the numeric user ID from `gh api user --jq .id`, not the
# username (usernames can be renamed). Unset or empty means nobody can sign in, and changing it
# signs out every existing session (the allowlist is re-checked on every request).
AUTH_ALLOWED_GITHUB_ID=

# ─── API token ── Next signs with it (TASK-003); FastAPI verifies it (TASK-004) ────────────
# Shared by Next's server code (signs a short-lived JWT per API call) and FastAPI (verifies it).
# Separate from AUTH_SECRET so each can rotate alone. At least 32 characters, or every API call
# but health throws: `openssl rand -base64 33`.
API_JWT_SECRET=

# ─── Optional local overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where Next's server code finds FastAPI. Default http://127.0.0.1:8000 (what `pnpm dev` runs).
# On Vercel the service binding injects it (vercel.json).
# API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Raw data lake location. Default ./data at the repo root; s3:// (R2) isn't supported yet.
# LAKE_URI=./data

# ─── Don't set these here ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set by tooling or a platform; putting them in .env.local changes what local commands do.
#   APP_ENV=test       Playwright and pytest set it: the API then reads TEST_DATABASE_URL.
#   FIXTURE_NOW        The fixed test clock; honored only when APP_ENV=test.
#   LIVE=true          Production only: destructive commands (rebuild, truncate, seed) refuse.
#   GIT_COMMIT_SHA     Reported by /api/py/health; e2e sets it, Vercel uses VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA.

# ─── Lives elsewhere (reference only) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel, Production:  DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED (Neon integration), LIVE=true,
#                      AUTH_SECRET (its own value), AUTH_GITHUB_ID/SECRET ("CFB Model" app),
#                      AUTH_ALLOWED_GITHUB_ID, API_JWT_SECRET (from TASK-003).
# Vercel, Preview:     DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED (per-PR Neon branch, integration),
#                      PRODUCTION_DATABASE_HOST (the preview build refuses to migrate it),
#                      AUTH_SECRET (its own value; minted sessions only, D-102),
#                      AUTH_ALLOWED_GITHUB_ID, API_JWT_SECRET (from TASK-003).
#                      No AUTH_GITHUB_ID/SECRET: previews have no GitHub sign-in (D-102).
# GitHub Actions secrets:   VERCEL_TOKEN, NEON_API_KEY, PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED
#                           (TASK-005); BACKUP_DATABASE_URL, R2_BACKUPS_ACCESS_KEY_ID,
#                           R2_BACKUPS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (TASK-006); PREVIEW_AUTH_SECRET,
#                           VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET (TASK-008).
# GitHub Actions variables: VERCEL_ORG_ID, VERCEL_PROJECT_ID, NEON_PROJECT_ID, PRODUCTION_URL
#                           (TASK-005); R2_ACCOUNT_ID, R2_BUCKET (TASK-006).
#                           Identifiers, not credentials: useless without the token or key.
